---
/**
 * Installation: a prompt that has a coding agent set Satin up, then the same steps by hand
 * (shadcn CLI or the npm package).
 */
import Docs from '../layouts/Docs.astro'
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro'
import Chip from '../components/Chip.astro'
import { page } from '../nav'
import CodeFrame from '../components/CodeFrame.astro'

const componentsJson = `{
  "$schema": "https://ui.shadcn.com/schema.json",
  "style": "new-york",
  "rsc": false,
  "tsx": true,
  "tailwind": {
    "config": "",
    "css": "",
    "baseColor": "neutral",
    "cssVariables": true,
    "prefix": ""
  },
  "aliases": {
    "components": "@/components",
    "ui": "@/components/ui",
    "lib": "@/lib",
    "utils": "@/lib/utils",
    "hooks": "@/hooks"
  }
}`
const alias = `// tsconfig.json (and tsconfig.app.json in Vite apps)
"compilerOptions": {
  "paths": { "@/*": ["./src/*"] }
}

// vite.config.ts
resolve: { alias: { '@': path.resolve(import.meta.dirname, 'src') } }`
const registryUsage = `// main.tsx, once for the whole app
import './styles/satin.css'

// App.tsx
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button'

export function Save() {
  return <Button>Save changes</Button>
}`
const packageUsage = `// main.tsx, once for the whole app
import '@satin/ui/styles.css'

// App.tsx
import { Button } from '@satin/ui/button'

export function Save() {
  return <Button>Save changes</Button>
}`
const agentPrompt = `Set up the Satin design system (https://uisatin.dev) in this React project.

1. Check the project uses React 19 or newer. Satin doesn't need Tailwind; don't add it.
2. Add an "@/*" import alias pointing at ./src in tsconfig.json (and tsconfig.app.json in a Vite app), and resolve "@" to src in the bundler config.
3. Write components.json at the project root by hand (shadcn init stops without Tailwind): style "new-york", rsc false, tsx true, empty Tailwind config and css paths, baseColor "neutral", cssVariables true, and aliases components "@/components", ui "@/components/ui", lib "@/lib", utils "@/lib/utils", hooks "@/hooks".
4. Install the components this project needs with the shadcn CLI, from Satin's registry: npx shadcn@latest add https://uisatin.dev/r/<name>.json. The full list is at https://uisatin.dev/r/registry.json. Start with button.
5. Import the styles once at the entry point: import './styles/satin.css'. Load the Geist and Geist Mono fonts, or the system font is used.
6. For dark mode, put the "dark" class on any parent element.
7. Use the components as they come. Colour, radius, type and motion come from Satin's tokens; don't restyle them with raw values.

When you're done, render a Button to check the styles load, and tell me what you installed.`
const h2 = 'text-lg font-medium text-text-default'
const h3 = 'text-base leading-6 font-medium text-text-default'
const prose = 'text-base leading-6 text-text-muted'
const link = 'rounded-sm text-text-default underline underline-offset-2 focus-visible:shadow-border-focus focus-visible:outline-none'
---

<Docs current="installation">
  <PageHeader id="installation" title={page('installation').title} description={page('installation').description} />

  <section aria-labelledby="agent-title" class="flex flex-col gap-3 pt-4">
    <h2 id="agent-title" class={h2}>Install with your agent</h2>
    <p class={prose}>
      Paste this prompt into Claude Code, Cursor or any coding agent that works in your repository. It sets up the import
      alias and <Chip>components.json</Chip>, installs components from Satin's registry and loads the styles, the same
      steps as below.
    </p>
    <CodeFrame code={agentPrompt} label="Prompt" lang="md" copyLabel="Copy prompt" wrap />
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="manual-title" class="flex flex-col gap-3 pt-10">
    <h2 id="manual-title" class={h2}>Install by hand</h2>
    <p class={prose}>Satin needs React 19 or newer. Fonts: the tokens ask for Geist and Geist Mono; load them, or the system font is used.</p>

    <h3 class:list={[h3, 'pt-3']}>Copy components with the shadcn CLI</h3>
    <p class={prose}>
      Every component is a <a class={link} href="https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/registry">shadcn registry</a> item. The CLI copies its source into <Chip>components/ui</Chip>, with the components it builds on, the <Chip>cn</Chip> helper and Satin’s precompiled styles, and installs its npm dependencies. Set your project up once:
    </p>
    <ol class="flex list-decimal flex-col gap-3 pl-5 text-base leading-6 text-text-muted marker:text-text-subtle">
      <li>
        <p class="pb-3">Add the <Chip>@/</Chip> import alias, pointing at <Chip>src</Chip>.</p>
        <CodeFrame code={alias} label="Import alias" />
      </li>
      <li>
        <p class="pb-3">
          Add a <Chip>components.json</Chip> at the root of the project. Write it by hand: <Chip>shadcn init</Chip> stops when it can’t find Tailwind, and Satin doesn’t need it, so the Tailwind paths stay empty.
        </p>
        <CodeFrame code={componentsJson} label="components.json" lang="json" />
      </li>
      <li>
        <p class="pb-3">Add components by URL. Each component page has its own command under Installation.</p>
        <CodeFrame code="npx shadcn@latest add https://uisatin.dev/r/button.json" label="Terminal" lang="bash" copyLabel="Copy command" />
      </li>
      <li>
        <p class="pb-3">Import the styles once, then use the components.</p>
        <CodeFrame code={registryUsage} label="Usage" />
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h3 class:list={[h3, 'pt-6']} id="npm">Install the npm package</h3>
    <p class={prose}>
      <Chip>@satin/ui</Chip> ships compiled ES modules with types and <Chip>styles.css</Chip>. Every component has its own entry point, so you only ship what you use. Until it is published, build it from the Satin repository with <Chip>npm run build:ui</Chip> and install the <Chip>packages/ui/dist</Chip> folder.
    </p>
    <CodeFrame code="npm i @satin/ui" label="Terminal" lang="bash" copyLabel="Copy command" />
    <CodeFrame code={packageUsage} label="Usage" />
  </section>
</Docs>
